# WNC Exchange — design rules

## Layout & hierarchy

- One job per section: one headline, one short supporting sentence, one primary action.
- Home event block: **full-width upcoming** first (with compact schedule), **past events below** in a 2-up grid (1-up on mobile)—do not use equal 3-card grids for mixed upcoming/past.
- Steer users to dedicated pages for deep content. Prefer `/events/[slug]` for full schedule over stuffing interactive timelines into dialogs.

## Schedules

- Interactive horizontal timeline is the program UI for Nov 13.
- **Home:** `size="compact"` + `brief` + `showDetail={false}` — day-at-a-glance track only; CTAs below steer to the event page.
- **Event page:** `size="full"` — primary content, not an afterthought under placeholders.
- Always show a short hint that the track scrolls sideways and sessions are selectable.
- Design for touch: horizontal scroll with `overscroll-behavior-x: contain`; stack CTAs full-width under ~640px.

## Modals

- Keep modals for **issues** and **schools** practice browsing (established pattern).
- Do **not** put the interactive day schedule in home event modals—too easy to miss.
- If a surface needs a modal, keep it light: summary + short list + link to the full page.

## Mobile

- Check every new section at ~390px and ~768px before calling work done.
- Prefer single-column stacks; avoid side-by-side text+actions that squeeze on small screens.
- Past-event cards: image + copy grid that collapses cleanly; clamp long summaries.

## Content & dates

- Canonical upcoming event: **Friday, November 13, 2026 · Mars Hill University**.
- Do not invent a 6th award winner or contest name—use working titles until sponsors confirm.
- Single registration URL via `site.registerUrl` (no scattered `example.com` when a real link exists).

## Visual language

- Preserve existing tokens (`--purple`, `--blue`, `--green`, `--cream`, Source Serif / Source Sans).
- Avoid purple-on-white AI clichés, heavy multi-shadow cards, and floating promo badges on hero faces.
- Hero location chips (e.g. “UNCA campus”, Brain Hub org) stay on the media layer corners—not overlay stickers on people.

## Process

- Work one workstream at a time; pause for human verify + commit between streams.
- Prefer small, testable UI increments; run `npm run build` after structural page changes.
